# scripts/opcount: NR1's receipt (NAMED-ROWS): `namedrowbench bench named N`
# makes N calls that fail a named row of six (sql's Lost) six times in
# seven, catches the failure as the row value and matches it by the name
# (Go's error since NR1); the cost of one call is the slope between the two
# sizes. The control maps each failure with an errors.As chain, as hand Go
# does. The sealed form is this workload's program built with
# -ldflags=-X=ergo.local/prototype/internal/sketch/lower.namedRowLowering=sealed.
unit call
sizes 409600 2457600
args bench named {n}
control benchmarks/namedrow/testdata/control
